  "question": {
    "text": "Let the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be rotated through a right angle about its line of intersection with the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. If the mirror image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in the rotated plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the equation of the rotated plane be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>This plane is perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>So the equation of rotated plane will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also given that the mirror image of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;in rotated plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p>Let coordinate of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So midpoint of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>This point&nbsp;will lie on the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}